Worked measurement examples — JCGM GUM-5:2026 (@met-examples: 0, is #book, #part-of @met-sources) { r_4FVN1GYTH9X8M1JFWFNT696GR0
JCGM GUM-5:2026. Guide to the expression of uncertainty in measurement — Part 5: Examples. [Official edition DOI](https://doi.org/10.59161/YNLY8209) · [Catalogue](https://www.bipm.org/en/committees/jc/jcgm/publications).

Read the complete volume in stages. Begin with chapter 1, Measurement of pH: linear interpolation. Compare chapter 2, Determination of benzo[a]pyrene, for contrasting propagation approaches. Use chapter 4, Gravimetric mixture preparation and calculation of composition, when studying correlated outputs. The remaining examples extend the advanced reading and provide cases to reconstruct independently.

The chemical examples illustrate general model and uncertainty questions, but their material-specific methods require chemistry preparation. They are reading and calculation studies, not instructions to handle hazardous analytes unsupervised.

The inspected first edition is a 145-page PDF with JCGM copyright and reproduction/translation terms. Catalogue, contents, and publication identity checked on 28 October 2026. It remains an authorized external reference.

